---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/classic-pages.css';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { papers, categories, meta, formatDate, pathFor, repoUrl } from '../lib/catalog';
import { MAJOR_CATEGORIES, QUADRANTS, QUADRANT_STATUSES, taxonomyLabel } from '../lib/taxonomy.mjs';
const topicMissingCount = papers.filter(paper => paper.primaryCategory === 'Uncategorized').length;
const majorMissingCount = papers.filter(paper => paper.majorCategory === null).length;
const quadrantCount = papers.filter(paper => QUADRANTS.some(quadrant => quadrant === paper.quadrant)).length;
const otherQuadrantLabels = QUADRANT_STATUSES.filter(value => !QUADRANTS.includes(value)).map(taxonomyLabel).join(', ');
const dates = papers.map(paper => paper.submittedDate).filter((date): date is string => Boolean(date)).sort();
const years = papers.map(paper => paper.publicationYear).filter((year): year is number => Number.isInteger(year)).sort((a, b) => a - b);
const firstDate = dates[0];
const lastDate = dates.at(-1);
const collectionStart = firstDate ? formatDate(firstDate, { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' }) : null;
const collectionEnd = lastDate ? formatDate(lastDate, { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' }) : null;
---

<BaseLayout title="About the collection" description="A community resource for discovering research on World-Action Models, sharing papers, and exploring connections across the field." active="about">
  <div class="shell about-page">
    <header class="about-header"><h1>About the collection</h1><p>A community reading list on world models, prediction, planning, and control.</p></header>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-body">
        <section aria-labelledby="scope-heading"><span class="section-number">01 / SCOPE</span><h2 id="scope-heading">Where world models meet action</h2><p>The collection connects foundational work, vision-language-action models, World-Action Models, datasets, evaluation metrics, benchmarks or simulators, core components, and related resources. These resources support the study of prediction, planning, and control.</p><p>Browse by major category and subcategory, compare model approaches in the quadrant view, or search for an idea or author. Each entry links to its original research source, with PDF, DOI, code, and project links when recorded.</p></section>

        <section aria-labelledby="organization-heading"><span class="section-number">02 / ORGANIZATION</span><h2 id="organization-heading">Three ways into the collection</h2><p>The <a href={`${pathFor('map/')}?mode=major`}>{MAJOR_CATEGORIES.length} major categories</a> organize entries by their main contribution. Subcategories describe more specific roles and connections.{majorMissingCount === 0 ? <> Every entry currently has a recorded major category.</> : <> {majorMissingCount} entries have no major category recorded and remain in the library.</>}</p><p>The <a href={`${pathFor('map/')}?mode=quadrants`}>quadrant view</a> crosses architecture—One Model or Dual-system—with prediction paradigm—joint prediction or inverse dynamics (IDM). {quadrantCount} entries are recorded in Q1–Q4. The remaining states—{otherQuadrantLabels}—are kept separate. Joint training alone does not establish a One Model architecture.</p><p>The <a href={`${pathFor('map/')}?mode=topics`}>{categories.length} original research topics</a> remain available as a separate thematic view.{topicMissingCount > 0 && <> {topicMissingCount} entries have no original Primary Category recorded; this does not mean their major category, subcategories, or quadrant are missing.</>}</p><p>Components of WAMs contains core encoders, pretrained backbones, tokenizers, and canonical action heads, such as VAE, CLIP, DINO, Wan, and Cosmos. Using a component does not make a complete WAM or a task-specific training method a component. Foundational work is limited to historically foundational research first published before 2026. Related resources collects relevant surveys, runtimes, supporting representations, and adjacent research. Dedicated neural simulators belong in Benchmarks & simulators. Explicit category reviews draw on the reading evidence and remain authoritative during synchronization. Source-review status and architecture or prediction-paradigm judgments remain separate; unsupported assignments stay unresolved. Missing abstracts and dates remain unfilled; recorded BibTeX can be copied from a detail page. Submission dates and publication years are shown separately, and year filters use only recorded years.</p><a class="text-link" href={pathFor('map/')}>Explore the research map <Icon name="right" size={17}/></a></section>

        <section aria-labelledby="contribute-heading"><span class="section-number">03 / CONTRIBUTE</span><h2 id="contribute-heading">Help the collection grow</h2><p>Found a relevant paper or a detail that needs updating? Open an issue on GitHub. A useful submission includes the title, authors, source link, and suggested major category or subcategories when known.</p><p>For classification corrections, include the paper link, the field to update, and supporting research sources. Maintainers record accepted category reviews locally or update the Notion source before exporting it. Accepted updates appear in the catalog and project website.</p><div class="contribution-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={`${repoUrl}/issues/new/choose`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Suggest a paper <Icon name="plus" size={16}/></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Icon name="github" size={16}/> Visit the repository <Icon name="arrow" size={14}/></a></div></section>
      </div>

      <aside class="collection-sidebar" aria-label="Collection overview">
        <div class="collection-card"><span class="eyebrow">THE COLLECTION</span><div class="collection-stat"><strong>{papers.length}</strong><span>research entries</span></div><div class="collection-stat"><strong>{MAJOR_CATEGORIES.length}</strong><span>major categories</span></div><p class="collection-pending">{quadrantCount} entries recorded in Q1–Q4</p><dl>{years.length > 0 && <div><dt>Recorded publication years</dt><dd>{years[0]}{years[0] !== years.at(-1) && ` – ${years.at(-1)}`}</dd></div>}{collectionStart && collectionEnd && <div><dt>Known submission dates</dt><dd>{collectionStart === collectionEnd ? collectionStart : <>{collectionStart}<br/><span class="coverage-to">to</span> {collectionEnd}</>}</dd></div>}<div><dt>Collection updated</dt><dd><time datetime={meta.updatedAt}>{formatDate(meta.updatedAt.slice(0, 10))}</time></dd></div></dl><a href={`${pathFor('papers/')}#library`}>Browse the library <Icon name="right" size={16}/></a></div>
        <p class="sidebar-note">Date ranges cover only records with the corresponding date or year.</p>
        <p class="sidebar-note">Follow the repository for additions and updates. Suggest papers and corrections through GitHub Issues.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @layer components {
  .about-page { padding-top:65px; padding-bottom:85px; }
  .about-header { max-width:750px; padding-bottom:48px; }
  h1 { color:#1f3c55; font-size:calc(clamp(34px,4.2vw,49px) * var(--font-scale)); line-height:1.16; letter-spacing:-1.7px; font-weight:600; margin:19px 0 21px; }
  h1 span { color:#718ba2; }
  .about-header > p { max-width:580px; color:#778593; font-size:calc(14px * var(--font-scale)); line-height:1.9; margin:0; }
  .about-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 270px; gap:90px; padding-top:37px; border-top:1px solid #e2e8ed; }
  .about-body { max-width:665px; }
  .about-body section + section { margin-top:43px; padding-top:34px; border-top:1px solid #e6ebef; }
  .section-number { font-size:calc(9px * var(--font-scale)); font-weight:500; letter-spacing:1.2px; color:#91a0ad; }
  h2 { color:#2e4a62; font-size:calc(23px * var(--font-scale)); font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.5px; margin:12px 0 17px; line-height:1.35; }
  .about-body p { color:#74818e; font-size:calc(13px * var(--font-scale)); line-height:1.95; margin:0 0 15px; }
  .about-body p a { color:#496e90; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px; }
  .collection-pending { grid-column:1/-1; margin:18px 0 0; color:#8a96a1; font-size:calc(11px * var(--font-scale)); }
  .text-link { display:inline-flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; color:#496e90; text-decoration:none; font-size:calc(12px * var(--font-scale)); margin-top:3px; }
  .text-link:hover { color:#183e60; }
  .contribution-actions { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px; margin-top:24px; }
  .collection-card { border:1px solid #dfe7ed; border-radius:5px; background:white; padding:26px; }
  .collection-card > .eyebrow { font-size:calc(9px * var(--font-scale)); }
  .collection-stat { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:3px; margin-top:21px; }
  .collection-stat strong { font-size:calc(37px * var(--font-scale)); letter-spacing:-1.2px; font-weight:500; line-height:1.1; color:#3f607c; }
  .collection-stat > span { font-size:calc(11px * var(--font-scale)); color:#8795a1; }
  dl { border-top:1px solid #e7edf1; margin:25px 0 0; padding-top:22px; }
  dl > div + div { margin-top:21px; }
  dt { font-size:calc(9px * var(--font-scale)); color:#98a2ad; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.9px; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:7px; }
  dd { margin:0; font-size:calc(12px * var(--font-scale)); line-height:1.7; color:#61788c; }
  .coverage-to { color:#9aa5af; }
  .collection-card > a { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; color:#60819d; font-size:calc(11px * var(--font-scale)); text-decoration:none; border-top:1px solid #e7edf1; margin-top:24px; padding-top:20px; }
  .sidebar-note { margin:15px 13px 0; font-size:calc(10px * var(--font-scale)); line-height:1.9; color:#98a3ae; }
  @media (max-width:900px) { .about-grid { gap:40px; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 240px; }.collection-card { padding:23px; } }
  @media (max-width:650px) { .about-page { padding-top:40px; padding-bottom:55px; }.about-header { padding-bottom:34px; }h1 { letter-spacing:-1px; }.about-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; padding-top:28px; gap:38px; }.about-body { max-width:none; }h2 { font-size:calc(21px * var(--font-scale)); }.collection-card { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:0 25px; }.collection-card > .eyebrow,.collection-card dl,.collection-card > a { grid-column:1/-1; }.collection-card dl { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:20px; }dl > div + div { margin-top:0; } }
  }
</style>
